.\" Manpage for mitsubishicheck
.\" Contact: security@example.com
.TH MITSUBISHICHECK 1 "January 2024" "1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mitsubishicheck \- Security audit tool for Mitsubishi PLCs using MELSEC protocol
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mitsubishicheck
[\fB\-t\fR \fITARGET\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fIPORT\fR]
[\fB\-\-network\fR \fINETWORK\fR]
[\fB\-\-checks\fR \fICHECKS\fR]
[\fB\-\-all\-checks\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR]
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mitsubishicheck
is a comprehensive security assessment tool for Mitsubishi Programmable
Logic Controllers (PLCs) using the MELSEC Communication Protocol.
.PP
The tool performs various security checks including authentication testing,
memory access verification, CVE detection, and protocol security analysis.
.PP
.B WARNING:
This tool is intended for authorized security testing only. Unauthorized
access to computer systems is illegal. Industrial Control Systems control
physical processes - improper testing can cause equipment damage or safety hazards.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Target Specification"
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target " " \fIIP\fR
Target PLC IP address to scan.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Target port number. Default: 5007.
.TP
.BR \-\-network " " \fICIDR\fR
Network range to scan in CIDR notation (e.g., 192.168.1.0/24).
.TP
.BR \-\-ports " " \fIPORTS\fR
Port specification for network scans. Supports single ports (5007),
ranges (5000-5010), and lists (5007,5006,5010).
.SS "Check Selection"
.TP
.BR \-\-checks " " \fICHECKS\fR
Comma-separated list of security checks to run.
Available checks: discovery, authentication, memory, firmware, cve,
protocol, control, information.
.TP
.BR \-\-all\-checks
Run all available security checks.
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude\-checks " " \fICHECKS\fR
Comma-separated list of checks to exclude.
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-checks
List all available security checks and exit.
.SS "Check Options"
.TP
.BR \-\-test\-write
Enable memory write testing. USE WITH EXTREME CAUTION - this writes
to PLC memory and may affect system operation.
.TP
.BR \-\-fuzz
Enable protocol fuzzing. MAY CAUSE DEVICE INSTABILITY - only use
in isolated test environments.
.TP
.BR \-\-default\-passwords
Test for default and common passwords.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-password\-attempts " " \fINUM\fR
Maximum password attempts for brute force testing. Default: 10.
.SS "Output Options"
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Output report file path. Format is auto-detected from extension.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format. Options: text, json, html, csv, markdown. Default: text.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity. Can be specified multiple times (-v, -vv, -vvv).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Quiet mode - only show findings, suppress informational messages.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output.
.SS "Connection Options"
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
Connection timeout in seconds. Default: 5.0.
.TP
.BR \-\-udp
Use UDP instead of TCP for communication.
.TP
.BR \-\-frame " " \fITYPE\fR
MELSEC frame type: 3E (QnA compatible) or 4E (iQ-R). Default: 3E.
.SS "Other Options"
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Show program version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-disclaimer
Show full legal disclaimer and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.SH SECURITY CHECKS
.TP
.B discovery
Check for exposed MELSEC services and ports. Identifies open ports,
protocol fingerprints, and UDP service exposure.
.TP
.B authentication
Check for authentication weaknesses including missing password protection,
default credentials, and lockout mechanism testing.
.TP
.B memory
Check for unauthorized memory access. Tests read/write access to various
device memory areas including data registers, relays, and special registers.
.TP
.B firmware
Check for firmware vulnerabilities including known vulnerable versions,
end-of-life models, and version disclosure.
.TP
.B cve
Check against database of known CVE vulnerabilities affecting Mitsubishi PLCs.
.TP
.B protocol
Check for MELSEC protocol security weaknesses including cleartext
communication, replay attack susceptibility, and malformed packet handling.
.TP
.B control
Check for unauthorized access to dangerous PLC control functions like
RUN/STOP commands and program memory.
.TP
.B information
Check for sensitive information disclosure through device identification,
error messages, and memory content analysis.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Scan completed successfully, no critical/high findings.
.TP
.B 1
Error during scan (connection failure, invalid arguments, etc.).
.TP
.B 2
Scan completed with critical or high severity findings.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Scan a single PLC with default checks:
.B mitsubishicheck -t 192.168.1.100
.TP
Run all security checks:
.B mitsubishicheck -t 192.168.1.100 --all-checks
.TP
Scan a network range:
.B mitsubishicheck --network 192.168.1.0/24
.TP
Generate HTML report:
.B mitsubishicheck -t 192.168.1.100 -o report.html --all-checks
.TP
Run specific checks only:
.B mitsubishicheck -t 192.168.1.100 --checks authentication,cve
.TP
Test for default passwords:
.B mitsubishicheck -t 192.168.1.100 --default-passwords
.TP
Use UDP protocol:
.B mitsubishicheck -t 192.168.1.100 --udp --port 5006
.TP
Generate JSON report for SIEM:
.B mitsubishicheck -t 192.168.1.100 --format json -o findings.json
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mitsubishicheck/config.yaml
User configuration file (optional).
.TP
.I /etc/mitsubishicheck/config.yaml
System-wide configuration file (optional).
.SH SUPPORTED DEVICES
.PP
The tool supports the following Mitsubishi PLC series:
.IP \(bu 4
MELSEC iQ-R Series
.IP \(bu 4
MELSEC iQ-F Series
.IP \(bu 4
MELSEC-Q Series
.IP \(bu 4
MELSEC-L Series
.IP \(bu 4
MELSEC-QnA Series
.IP \(bu 4
FX Series (FX3, FX5)
.IP \(bu 4
MELSEC-A Series (legacy)
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.PP
This tool is designed for authorized security testing and assessment.
Consider the following:
.IP \(bu 4
Always obtain written authorization before testing
.IP \(bu 4
PLCs control physical processes - improper testing can be dangerous
.IP \(bu 4
Network segmentation is critical for ICS security
.IP \(bu 4
Test in isolated environments when possible
.IP \(bu 4
Some checks may affect PLC operation
